 "comment": "Cliff faces cut from the story maps of the ROM (MAP_BG) by Tools/pmd/extract_cliffs.py into Resources/Cliffs/<style>/<role>_<n>.png (24×24). map: the BMA name; layer: lower, upper (its transparent pixels kept) or both; pieces: per role, the top left corner (pixels) of each 24×24 piece in the rendered map (or {map, layer, at} from another map). Roles: top / middle / bottom (rows of a face, from the ground above it down; their variants are consecutive columns of the map, drawn in turn along the face), leftTop, leftBottom, rightTop, rightBottom (the ends of a face; middle rows use the bottom ones), stairsLeft/Mid/Right + Top/Bottom (stairs 3 tiles wide cut into a face), mouthLeft/Mid/Right + Top/Bottom (a cave's mouth in a face). ground: the map's ground cleared from the top of `roles` (samples: rectangles of its colours; tolerance; depth in pixels). mirror: a role made by flipping another. lip: rows of a piece (the level's edge seen from above) turned into back, left, right, backLeft, backRight, innerLeft, innerRight (the other sides of a level); ends: the ends of a face made from its first column and that lip. previewFloor: the ground colour of the preview. foot: how the bottom row of a face meets the ground (the map's ground cleared from its bottom, or a wavy cut). shadow: cast on the ground at a face's foot (alpha, depth in pixels). mirrorLoop: a face's columns then the same mirrored in reverse order (no seam where they repeat).",
